<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Gate-bound: carried by a dungeon boss that walked out with the final breach
    wave. Killing it on the colony map pays the same clear loot and clear XP as
    beating it in its own hall — see Hediff_GateBound for why the bounty rides
    the pawn instead of a tracker.

    Deliberately VISIBLE. A player who has just been handed a rank-S monster on
    their doorstep should be able to see that this particular creature is worth
    killing rather than merely surviving.

    No stages, no capMods, no tendable parts: it changes nothing about the pawn.
    It is a marker that happens to be readable.
  -->
  <HediffDef>
    <defName>IsekaiDungeons_GateBound</defName>
    <hediffClass>IsekaiDungeons.Hediff_GateBound</hediffClass>
    <label>gate-bound</label>
    <description>This creature is the master of a gate that has broken open. Whatever hoard its dungeon held is still tied to it — kill it and the dungeon settles its debt here, wherever it falls.</description>
    <defaultLabelColor>(0.85, 0.55, 0.95)</defaultLabelColor>
    <isBad>false</isBad>
    <scenarioCanAdd>false</scenarioCanAdd>
    <everCurableByItem>false</everCurableByItem>
    <maxSeverity>1.0</maxSeverity>
    <initialSeverity>1.0</initialSeverity>
  </HediffDef>

  <!--
    GATE SOVEREIGN. Only exists when Isekai Creatures is NOT installed: a
    stand-in boss (a vanilla creature filling in for a missing bestiary boss)
    is lifted to the boss threat measured in the Creatures-installed game.
    Hediff_GateSovereign builds its stage at runtime from the multiplier
    ThreatParity computed: toughness and melee damage split as square roots,
    or all toughness for a ranged boss. Visible so the player can see why this
    elk hits like a dragon.
  -->
  <HediffDef>
    <defName>IsekaiDungeons_GateSovereign</defName>
    <hediffClass>IsekaiDungeons.Hediff_GateSovereign</hediffClass>
    <label>gate sovereign</label>
    <description>The gate has crowned this creature its master. The dungeon's own power runs through it, hardening its body and driving its blows far beyond what its kind should manage.</description>
    <defaultLabelColor>(0.95, 0.75, 0.30)</defaultLabelColor>
    <isBad>false</isBad>
    <scenarioCanAdd>false</scenarioCanAdd>
    <everCurableByItem>false</everCurableByItem>
    <maxSeverity>1.0</maxSeverity>
    <initialSeverity>1.0</initialSeverity>
  </HediffDef>

</Defs>
